    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320-a9">

                <pb facs="0879" n="665" xml:id="pg665"/>

                <head>H.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 11, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Citizen Minister of Foreign Affairs</hi>: The citizen
                    General Juan N. Cortina, commanding the first brigade of Tamaulipas, in a
                    dispatch dated the 28th of August last, writes me as follows:</p>
                <p>“I have the honor to send you a copy of the power of attorney which the
                    foreigner, Champion, gave me in order to recover nine horses, which some bandits
                    had robbed from him in the State of Texas.”</p>
                <p>And I have the honor to transmit the above in reply to and as the result of your
                    dispatch on the subject, dated August 5, inclosing herewith a copy of the said
                    power of attorney.</p>
                <p>Independence and liberty!</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MEJIA.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d320-a9-a1.xml" xpointer="d320-a9-a1"/>
